menu "PlantHub Swarm"

config PLANTHUB_WIFI_COUNTRY
    string "WiFi regulatory domain / country code"
    default "01"
    help
        The regulatory domain determines which channels a node may sweep
        during pairing/resync, and which channel a main hub's WiFi
        association is allowed to sit on. "01" is the IDF's world-safe
        default and restricts operation to channels 1-11. An actual ISO
        country code for a region that permits channels 12-13 (most of
        the EU, including Switzerland) enables them -- without this, a
        node can never find a hub whose router happens to land on
        channel 12 or 13, a silent and permanent pairing failure.

        WARNING: setting a country code for a region these devices do
        not actually operate in is a regulatory violation. Only set this
        to a code that matches where the hardware will really be used.

endmenu
